I hinted the hot path where `type` is unset and the profile lookup succeeds, and cached the profile pointer to reduce repeated member loads. This keeps identical behavior while improving branch layout for typical decode calls.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(type != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 0))
        return type;

    const auto* const p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect((p != NULL) && (profileIndex < p->numFields), 1))
        return p->fields[profileIndex].type;

    return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;
}
```